CORE
assignment_value.c
--evaluation-order-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 12 the value of an assignment is the value stored: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 13 y == 1 regardless of evaluation order: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The assignment y = 1 and the call to g are indeterminately sequenced, so y is
1 or 2 afterwards. The value of the assignment expression is the value stored,
i.e., 1, whichever order is chosen.
